@riverio1e $CIEN was another company that explicitly cited bottlenecks with lasers last month... 

Wanlian Securities also flagged Ciena today as a candidate for supplier diversification following the $MRVL / $LITE acquisition... with other laser manufacturers gaining share.

So I think $SIVE has a tremendous opportunity for market capture in the coming months.

@steeluu To my knowledge, $CRDO doesn't have in-house CW DFB laser manufacturing capabilities, so not quite... 

Dustphotonics integrates external CW lasers so Credo is another potential $MRVL for the need to M&A laser companies.  

They did another with Hyperlume earlier but that was for microLEDs, not CW. Lot of industry channel checks like Largan cast a lot of doubts over that microLED commercialization for CPO (not every short reach application).

@jacobsimon2002 Well.. that was before $MRVL crashed. The deal is 4.5x Marvell shares for every Lumentum share. 

4.5x * 196 = $882 (floating), so you're getting that for $LITE, which is still more than current prices.  

If Marvell recovers, so does Lumentum shares now

@prashant_0723 the goal is to always minimum 2X the S&amp;P 500 every single year while keeping drawdowns very minimum.

For example, if S&amp;P 500 crashes -50%, we would only crash -25%. 

This is the goal. To make sure you never have to worry again for the core portfolio.
